      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "INTRODUCTION",
          "content": "Gallstone ileus is a rare complication of cholecystolithiasis. It causes 1-3% of the mechanical obstructions of the small bowel. It often affects patients between 63 and 85 years old. Pre-operative diagnosis is usually delayed 1-10 days because there is not a specific symptomatology."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CASE REPORT",
          "content": "The authors report the case of a 50 year-old man with diagnosis of mechanical obstruction of the small bowel caused by a voluminous gallstone. Ileal occlusion was showed by CT. The patient underwent to one-stage emergency surgery with enterolithotomy, cholecystectomy and duodenal fistula repair. Patient's recovery was regular and he was discharged fourteen days after surgery."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "DISCUSSION",
          "content": "In our case gallstone ileus was diagnosed with a delay of 5 days. Ultrasonography was not able to show the gallbladder. Diagnosis was made by CT, which is the diagnostic gold standard."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Patient's performance status influences surgical strategy. In our experience, the patient underwent one-stage surgery because he was considered at low risk. Instead staged procedure with enterolithotomy and delayed cholecystectomy and fistula repair, is performed only in patients at high risk."
        }
      ]},
